{"audio": "matthew-17.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 204400, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 2533, "text": "Matthew, Chapter Seventeen."}, {"start_ms": 2533, "end_ms": 14533, "text": "And after six days Jesus taketh Peter, James, and John his brother, and bringeth them up into an high mountain apart, And was transfigured before them: and his face did shine as the sun, and his raiment was white as the light."}, {"start_ms": 14533, "end_ms": 18533, "text": "And, behold, there appeared unto them Moses and Elias talking with him."}, {"start_ms": 18533, "end_ms": 30400, "text": "Then answered Peter, and said unto Jesus, Lord, it is good for us to be here: if thou wilt, let us make here three tabernacles; one for thee, and one for Moses, and one for Elias."}, {"start_ms": 30400, "end_ms": 42533, "text": "While he yet spake, behold, a bright cloud overshadowed them: and behold a voice out of the cloud, which said, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased; hear ye him."}, {"start_ms": 42533, "end_ms": 46933, "text": "And when the disciples heard it, they fell on their face, and were sore afraid."}, {"start_ms": 46933, "end_ms": 51333, "text": "And Jesus came and touched them, and said, Arise, and be not afraid."}, {"start_ms": 51333, "end_ms": 55600, "text": "And when they had lifted up their eyes, they saw no man, save Jesus only."}, {"start_ms": 55600, "end_ms": 63200, "text": "And as they came down from the mountain, Jesus charged them, saying, Tell the vision to no man, until the Son of man be risen again from the dead."}, {"start_ms": 63200, "end_ms": 68533, "text": "And his disciples asked him, saying, Why then say the scribes that Elias must first come?"}, {"start_ms": 68533, "end_ms": 74133, "text": "And Jesus answered and said unto them, Elias truly shall first come, and restore all things."}, {"start_ms": 74133, "end_ms": 82000, "text": "But I say unto you, That Elias is come already, and they knew him not, but have done unto him whatsoever they listed."}, {"start_ms": 82000, "end_ms": 85467, "text": "Likewise shall also the Son of man suffer of them."}, {"start_ms": 85467, "end_ms": 90000, "text": "Then the disciples understood that he spake unto them of John the Baptist."}, {"start_ms": 90000, "end_ms": 104400, "text": "And when they were come to the multitude, there came to him a certain man, kneeling down to him, and saying, Lord, have mercy on my son: for he is lunatick, and sore vexed: for ofttimes he falleth into the fire, and oft into the water."}, {"start_ms": 104400, "end_ms": 108000, "text": "And I brought him to thy disciples, and they could not cure him."}, {"start_ms": 108000, "end_ms": 114133, "text": "Then Jesus answered and said, O faithless and perverse generation, how long shall I be with you?"}, {"start_ms": 114133, "end_ms": 116133, "text": "how long shall I suffer you?"}, {"start_ms": 116133, "end_ms": 117867, "text": "bring him hither to me."}, {"start_ms": 117867, "end_ms": 123733, "text": "And Jesus rebuked the devil; and he departed out of him: and the child was cured from that very hour."}, {"start_ms": 123733, "end_ms": 129600, "text": "Then came the disciples to Jesus apart, and said, Why could not we cast him out?"}, {"start_ms": 129600, "end_ms": 144000, "text": "And Jesus said unto them, Because of your unbelief: for verily I say unto you, If ye have faith as a grain of mustard seed, ye shall say unto this mountain, Remove hence to yonder place; and it shall remove; and nothing shall be impossible unto you."}, {"start_ms": 144000, "end_ms": 147733, "text": "Howbeit this kind goeth not out but by prayer and fasting."}, {"start_ms": 147733, "end_ms": 158933, "text": "And while they abode in Galilee, Jesus said unto them, The Son of man shall be betrayed into the hands of men: And they shall kill him, and the third day he shall be raised again."}, {"start_ms": 158933, "end_ms": 160267, "text": "And they were exceeding sorry."}, {"start_ms": 160267, "end_ms": 168267, "text": "And when they were come to Capernaum, they that received tribute money came to Peter, and said, Doth not your master pay tribute?"}, {"start_ms": 168267, "end_ms": 170667, "text": "He saith, Yes."}, {"start_ms": 170667, "end_ms": 176267, "text": "And when he was come into the house, Jesus prevented him, saying, What thinkest thou, Simon?"}, {"start_ms": 176267, "end_ms": 179067, "text": "of whom do the kings of the earth take custom or tribute?"}, {"start_ms": 179067, "end_ms": 181733, "text": "of their own children, or of strangers?"}, {"start_ms": 181733, "end_ms": 184533, "text": "Peter saith unto him, Of strangers."}, {"start_ms": 184533, "end_ms": 188667, "text": "Jesus saith unto him, Then are the children free."}, {"start_ms": 188667, "end_ms": 204400, "text": "Notwithstanding, lest we should offend them, go thou to the sea, and cast an hook, and take up the fish that first cometh up; and when thou hast opened his mouth, thou shalt find a piece of money: that take, and give unto them for me and thee."}], "words": [{"t": "Matthew,", "s": 905, "e": 1246, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 1488, "e": 1849, "si": 0}, {"t": "Seventeen.", "s": 1910, "e": 2453, "si": 0}, {"t": "And", "s": 3054, "e": 3154, "si": 1}, {"t": "after", "s": 3174, "e": 3374, "si": 1}, {"t": "six", "s": 3435, "e": 3595, "si": 1}, {"t": "days", "s": 3715, "e": 3955, "si": 1}, {"t": "Jesus", "s": 4036, "e": 4356, "si": 1}, {"t": "taketh", "s": 4416, "e": 4697, "si": 1}, {"t": "Peter,", "s": 4737, "e": 5017, "si": 1}, {"t": "James,", "s": 5097, "e": 5398, "si": 1}, {"t": "and", "s": 5418, "e": 5498, "si": 1}, {"t": "John", "s": 5518, "e": 5738, "si": 1}, {"t": "his", "s": 5778, "e": 5879, "si": 1}, {"t": "brother,", "s": 5939, "e": 6219, "si": 1}, {"t": "and", "s": 6620, "e": 6700, "si": 1}, {"t": "bringeth", "s": 6720, "e": 7000, "si": 1}, {"t": "them", "s": 7020, "e": 7121, "si": 1}, {"t": "up", "s": 7161, "e": 7261, "si": 1}, {"t": "into", "s": 7301, "e": 7441, "si": 1}, {"t": "an", "s": 